+# Design
+
+## Context
+
+`parsePeriod` in `src/period.ts` only accepts midnight-UTC times and returns a day count; `src/rental.ts` prices through one shared function used by `quote` and `book`, and overlap checks already compare epoch milliseconds. See proposal.md for motivation.
+
+## Goals / Non-Goals
+
+**Goals:**
+- Hourly periods are priced at `hourlyPrice` per hour, in one place shared by quote and booking.
+- Hourly and whole-day bookings of one item conflict correctly.
+
+**Non-Goals:**
+- Hourly `availability` queries (it keeps whole-day periods; it already excludes items with overlapping hourly bookings), opening hours, minimum durations, discounts on hourly rentals.
+
+## Decisions
+
+- **Period kinds**: `parsePeriod` returns `{ startMs, endMs, days, hours }` style data plus a `kind`. Both times at midnight → whole-day (unchanged). Otherwise both must be on the hour and `end - start < 24h` → hourly. Anything else (e.g. 10:00 to 10:00 next day) is rejected. Availability keeps requiring whole-day periods, so it uses a whole-day-only mode of the parser.
+- **Pricing**: the shared pricing function branches on kind; hourly total = `hourlyPrice * hours`, no discount; throws when the item has no `hourlyPrice`.
+- **Overlap**: unchanged, millisecond-based, so hourly bookings block overlapping days and vice versa.
+- **Validation**: `hourlyPrice` is optional; when present it must be a non-negative safe integer. An `hourlyPrice` of 0 is allowed, like `dailyPrice`.
+
+## Risks / Trade-offs
+
+- [A period crossing midnight but under 24 hours was not specified] → treated as hourly, since it is shorter than a day and on the hour; recorded in the spec.
+- [A period of exactly 24 hours from midnight is a whole-day period] → priced daily.
